WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.203
[music playing]

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.876
[speaking spanish]

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:19.319
I'm not going to lie, it's
always a rush getting access

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.155
to these clandestine worlds.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.290
The cocaine pit,
the starting point

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:29.629
for such a storied black
market trade ranks up there.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.564
But as the reporter
high wears off,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:35.835
I realize that the whole process
boils down to brute labor

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.804
and simple chemistry.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.272
[speaking spanish]

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.009
So they've been doing
this for three days,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:46.813
and now this is the final step,
which they mix it with salt.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.351
It takes 400 kilos,
almost 900 pounds, of coca

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:54.788
leaves to make one
kilo of cocaine.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.124
They're soaked in water,
acid and bleach, which draws

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.859
the drugs out of the leaves.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.328
And now it's ready to
be moved on to smaller

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.130
containers to the lab.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.565
[speaking spanish]

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:09.102
[music playing]

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.315
Here in this
makeshift lab, they'll

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.017
start the purification process.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.486
[speaking spanish]

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.595
Researchers discovered how
to extract cocaine from coca

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:40.600
leaves over 150 years ago, and
Americans got their first taste

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.102
of the drug in Coca-Cola
back in the 19th

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:49.709
century before it was banned by
the federal government in 1914.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.345
It's a really,
really intense smell.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:56.316
[speaking spanish]

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:04.290
To purify cocaine in the
middle of the Peruvian jungle,

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.392
they figured out how
to extract the drug

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:11.698
using simple household chemicals
and a whole lot of gasoline.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:16.236
In this lab, each batch
requires 70 gallons.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.304
[speaking spanish]

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:31.751
Ammonia, bleach,
cement, lime, gasoline.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.821
With each toxic additive,
the drug becomes

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.357
more and more concentrated.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.359
So what they're doing is that
they're removing the top of it,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.194
which is the fuel,
and the bottom,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.096
there's a clear
sort of liquid, and

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.264
that's where the drug remains.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.933
Do you see it's pretty dark?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.038
And that's all the gasoline, and
the clear part now underneath.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:55.508
[speaking spanish]

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.711
So yeah, that's the
drugs right there.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.948
So they call that clear
liquid, they call it the soup.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.717
[speaking spanish]

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.123
[laughter]

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.524
They asked me if
I wanted to try it.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.425
[laughter]

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.126
I said no.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:16.362
[speaking spanish]

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.003
Oh, check this out.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.105
This is amazing.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.675
It's crazy to think that
only weeks from now,

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:34.480
this jungle soup will disappear
up some American's nostrils.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:38.885
Now it's time for the final
step, a splash of ammonia

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.853
to solidify the drugs.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.524
[speaking spanish]

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:47.293
OK, they have to speed it,
we have to speed it up, OK?

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.396
With so many livelihoods
depending on this lab,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.232
Civichia's friend is taking
a massive risk giving

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.501
us a peek behind the curtain.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:59.305
So when the chemist disappears
for a moment, I begin to worry.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.342
[speaking spanish]

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.019
OK, guys, we have
to go right now.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.722
[speaking spanish]

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:21.961
[tense music playing]

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.631
Let's go, let's go.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.000
His crew was spotted by
somebody up on the road.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:31.471
They say that we have to get
into the car get out of here.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.805
OK.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.307
We have to go fast.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.611
No, no, no.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:39.245
[speaking spanish]

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.113
Are they all inside?

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:43.049
[car engine]

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:47.186
[tense music playing]

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:54.694
Thankfully we escape
without incident,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:55.762
but the drugs long journey
north is only just beginning.

